1
00:02:19,476 --> 00:02:21,476


2
00:02:21,500 --> 00:02:26,920
That is why every king of this realm has been brave and strong.

3
00:02:29,520 --> 00:02:32,560
Just look at this king's heroic figure.

4
00:02:55,470 --> 00:02:58,560
The kings from long ago were so cool!

5
00:02:59,140 --> 00:03:03,520
Indeed, they were the bravest in the world! And this king too.

6
00:03:05,530 --> 00:03:08,660
So cool! Incredible!

7
00:03:21,750 --> 00:03:23,440
Hey, what about this king?

8
00:03:23,505 --> 00:03:25,453
Yes, he was strong too.

9
00:03:34,460 --> 00:03:36,206
Awesome!

10
00:03:41,270 --> 00:03:44,440
This is the sword the last king used to fight a dragon.

11
00:03:45,580 --> 00:03:47,640
And this helmet is from when the king

12
00:03:47,664 --> 00:03:50,913
before him fought a terrifying giant lion.

13
00:03:52,090 --> 00:03:54,940
As you can see, our kings were all valiant and strong.

14
00:03:55,351 --> 00:03:57,266
What about Sapphire?

15
00:03:58,020 --> 00:03:59,020
Well, you see...

16
00:04:01,350 --> 00:04:04,540
Sapphire will be the next king, right?

17
00:04:04,900 --> 00:04:09,360
Is Sapphire brave and strong too?

18
00:04:10,450 --> 00:04:13,613
Oh, far from it! Sapphire is neither brave nor strong.

19
00:04:13,873 --> 00:04:14,686
Why?

20
00:04:14,800 --> 00:04:16,860
Because Sapphire has yet to accomplish a feat

21
00:04:16,884 --> 00:04:19,200
worthy of display in this room.

22
00:04:19,700 --> 00:04:21,760
Yeah, Sapphire is all show.

23
00:04:21,880 --> 00:04:22,880
All show?

24
00:04:23,513 --> 00:04:24,980
Control yourself, Lord Sapphire!

25
00:04:25,004 --> 00:04:27,560
Getting angry here will only cause another mess.

26
00:04:27,780 --> 00:04:30,433
Dr. Uranai is keeping an eye on things, so you mustn't go out there.

27
00:04:31,000 --> 00:04:34,880
Is it all just for show? Is he actually a coward?

28
00:04:37,600 --> 00:04:40,300
A coward? Sapphire's a coward!

29
00:04:43,400 --> 00:04:46,400
He's a coward! Is Sapphire really a coward?

30
00:04:50,230 --> 00:04:51,780
Here comes the coward!

31
00:04:54,920 --> 00:04:58,794
Nylon said Sapphire is all talk and a coward—

32
00:04:58,818 --> 00:05:00,313
hey, stop that!

33
00:05:01,206 --> 00:05:03,500
Why, Lord Sapphire, Dr. Uranai

34
00:05:04,630 --> 00:05:07,746
Nylon, why do you say Sapphire is all talk and a coward?

35
00:05:08,860 --> 00:05:11,054
Because there isn't a single thing in this room

36
00:05:11,078 --> 00:05:13,400
that proves Lord Sapphire's courage.

37
00:05:13,735 --> 00:05:17,860
Sir Nylon, I will not tolerate such insolence toward Lord Sapphire!

38
00:05:18,980 --> 00:05:20,800
Then, Lord Sapphire, won't you show us

39
00:05:20,824 --> 00:05:23,620
this so-called courage for Lord Plastic's sake?

40
00:05:24,185 --> 00:05:25,547
Show it?

41
00:05:25,571 --> 00:05:28,434
Well... a deer called a Moose

42
00:05:28,458 --> 00:05:33,560
has settled in the forest near the castle. It's a monster ten meters tall.

43
00:05:33,919 --> 00:05:37,307
If that were all, it wouldn't be so bad,
but whenever hunters corner their prey,

44
00:05:37,331 --> 00:05:40,620
this giant deer appears, knocking them around

45
00:05:40,644 --> 00:05:44,240
and trampling them with its huge body and antlers.

46
00:05:44,615 --> 00:05:49,680
It steals all the leftover prey for itself and casually strolls off—a true villain.

47
00:05:49,906 --> 00:05:51,020
What do you think?

48
00:05:51,660 --> 00:05:54,140
Why don't we slay this evil stag?

49
00:05:54,620 --> 00:05:56,393
Is there really a wicked deer in that forest?

50
00:05:56,590 --> 00:05:58,200
All right, I'll go defeat them!

51
00:06:02,000 --> 00:06:03,000
Opal!

52
00:06:04,980 --> 00:06:07,419
Opal! He headed into the forest!

53
00:06:22,090 --> 00:06:24,353
Oh, Sapphire! Where are you going?

54
00:06:24,520 --> 00:06:26,800
Oh, Tink. Perfect timing.

55
00:06:27,000 --> 00:06:29,713
Is that the forest with the giant deer called Moose?

56
00:06:29,865 --> 00:06:31,420
Moose? Yeah, that's right.

57
00:06:31,493 --> 00:06:32,039
Thank you!

58
00:06:32,180 --> 00:06:33,833
Hey, wait up!

59
00:06:34,025 --> 00:06:36,180
That's so mean!

60
00:06:36,665 --> 00:06:38,620
But what was that about? Where are they going?

61
00:06:39,320 --> 00:06:41,086
It'll be a disaster if she gets beaten by Moose!

62
00:06:48,975 --> 00:06:50,469
It's pitch black in the forest.

63
00:06:50,494 --> 00:06:53,406
Opal, this is far enough. I'll search on my own from here.

64
00:07:06,460 --> 00:07:08,420
Hey, you guys. Have you seen Moose?

65
00:07:10,800 --> 00:07:12,673
Have you guys seen Moose?

66
00:07:14,720 --> 00:07:17,600
That's odd... Why is everyone running away?

67
00:07:19,254 --> 00:07:21,686
No playing tricks!

68
00:07:21,890 --> 00:07:23,420
Wait!

69
00:07:28,050 --> 00:07:29,100
Now I'm mad!

70
00:07:29,400 --> 00:07:30,640
Wait!

71
00:07:36,475 --> 00:07:37,760
How hasty!

72
00:07:41,240 --> 00:07:42,440
Look! Stop messing around!

73
00:07:49,730 --> 00:07:53,080
Monster Moose! Because of you, no one can enter this forest!

74
00:07:53,295 --> 00:07:55,020
Now Sapphire will vanquish you!

75
00:08:02,310 --> 00:08:04,006
If you try to run, you won't get away!

76
00:08:11,290 --> 00:08:12,290
This thing's huge!

77
00:08:22,660 --> 00:08:24,120
Now try this!

78
00:08:43,446 --> 00:08:45,433
What are you doing!?

79
00:08:51,866 --> 00:08:55,211
Please let Lord Sapphire be safe... 

80
00:08:55,235 --> 00:09:00,153
I'm so worried... I'm worried... I'm worried...

81
00:09:02,489 --> 00:09:04,293
Ah, you made it back...

82
00:09:08,999 --> 00:09:11,500
Oh, Lord Sapphire, are you hurt?

83
00:09:11,799 --> 00:09:15,580
Yeah, I totally lost. It sent me flying with its horns and I got knocked out.

84
00:09:16,000 --> 00:09:19,144
Oh, dear. So even Lord Sapphire failed?

85
00:09:19,168 --> 00:09:22,800
If I'd been there, I wouldn't have let them off so easily.

86
00:09:22,860 --> 00:09:27,746
It's no use. Even with Dr. Uranai here, Moose's head alone is this big.

87
00:09:27,790 --> 00:09:30,360
His head alone is this...

88
00:09:34,679 --> 00:09:38,120
Well, Lord Sapphire? Where is the moose's head?

89
00:09:38,630 --> 00:09:42,040
In the forest! I've spared their lives for another two or three days!

90
00:09:43,420 --> 00:09:45,940
Such impressive bravado!

91
00:09:46,305 --> 00:09:47,305
Shut up!

92
00:09:47,475 --> 00:09:50,840
What if... just what if you can't...

93
00:09:51,089 --> 00:09:52,940
When that time comes, I'll never pick up a sword again!

94
00:09:53,295 --> 00:09:56,346
So what will you do if Sapphire gets Moose to surrender?

95
00:09:56,660 --> 00:10:01,280
Indeed. Perhaps I'll go do a handstand on top of that tower. Just like that!

96
00:10:05,799 --> 00:10:09,126
Yeah, that's hilarious. Better practice while you still can.

97
00:10:09,270 --> 00:10:12,180
Lord Sapphire, let's go. Don't waste your time on a guy like him.

98
00:10:14,240 --> 00:10:16,835
Nylon, are you sure you should make such a promise?

99
00:10:16,859 --> 00:10:20,395
It's Sapphire we're talking about. If he gets serious, he might actually kill him.

100
00:10:20,419 --> 00:10:23,126
That's as it may be, but I have plenty of tricks up my sleeve.

101
00:10:25,489 --> 00:10:26,660
Do you know what this is?

102
00:10:27,045 --> 00:10:28,045
What is that?

103
00:10:28,539 --> 00:10:29,136
Stop!

104
00:10:29,160 --> 00:10:31,620
If the tip so much as touches someone, it'll drive them mad.

105
00:10:33,120 --> 00:10:35,960
It's a poisoned blowdart used by African natives.

106
00:10:36,245 --> 00:10:38,000
I'll jab this right into her neck.

107
00:10:38,760 --> 00:10:40,860
Now, now, just leave it to me.

108
00:11:32,487 --> 00:11:35,806
Damn it! I'm really off my game today!

109
00:11:35,900 --> 00:11:40,180
Lord Sapphire, are you alright? It's dawn already. Let's stop here.

110
00:11:40,825 --> 00:11:42,233
No, no! One more time!

111
00:11:42,459 --> 00:11:45,282
But... knocking you down any further...

112
00:11:45,306 --> 00:11:46,106
I said, again!

113
00:11:46,160 --> 00:11:47,080
Oh, fine...

114
00:12:07,404 --> 00:12:08,269
It's no good.

115
00:12:09,079 --> 00:12:10,580
Are you injured?

116
00:12:15,728 --> 00:12:18,000
At this rate, I'll never beat Moose.

117
00:12:18,365 --> 00:12:20,040
Sapphire won't even be able to hold a sword soon.

118
00:12:36,609 --> 00:12:40,600
Send up the second batch of smoke! More, more!

119
00:12:41,509 --> 00:12:43,220
Lord Nylon, we are ready!

120
00:12:43,675 --> 00:12:44,673
All right, begin!

121
00:12:50,740 --> 00:12:52,106
Hey, what are you standing around for?!

122
00:12:52,130 --> 00:12:53,959
Get that smoke into the forest, quick!

123
00:12:54,229 --> 00:12:55,640
And drive the beasts out!

124
00:12:55,889 --> 00:12:56,889
It'll be over soon.

125
00:13:35,185 --> 00:13:37,460
Hey, it's about time you came out!

126
00:13:44,689 --> 00:13:47,879
Don't kill it! Surround it with spears so it can't escape!

127
00:14:15,189 --> 00:14:16,540
It's a monster, just like the rumors say.

128
00:14:16,739 --> 00:14:18,979
Hey, everyone! It calmed down! Don't move!

129
00:14:20,279 --> 00:14:23,040
No matter what monster it is, it's no match for this!

130
00:14:49,665 --> 00:14:51,540
Good, the poison is taking effect!

131
00:15:05,060 --> 00:15:08,440
Until that poison wears off, Moose will go completely wild.

132
00:15:09,185 --> 00:15:11,840
Even Sapphire will end up trampled to death.

133
00:15:30,170 --> 00:15:31,320
That's Moose!

134
00:15:35,259 --> 00:15:37,413
Hey Moose! Where on earth are you going?

135
00:15:38,399 --> 00:15:39,960
Watch out, Hitsuji-san! Move!

136
00:15:54,686 --> 00:15:56,720
What is this, this glowing thing?

137
00:16:07,459 --> 00:16:09,560
Oh no! Moose has gone crazy!

138
00:16:20,180 --> 00:16:24,960
Moose is running wild in town, and the soldiers can't handle him at all!

139
00:16:25,315 --> 00:16:29,533
So, that's why we'd love for Lord Sapphire to come...

140
00:16:29,997 --> 00:16:31,066
Perfect timing.

141
00:16:31,090 --> 00:16:33,500
I've finally figured out a way to beat Moose.

142
00:16:34,165 --> 00:16:37,480
If a moose has two horns, Sapphire has three swords!

143
00:16:38,220 --> 00:16:39,540
Your Highness...

144
00:16:40,975 --> 00:16:44,373
Drop your sword and I won't force you to come with us.

145
00:16:45,479 --> 00:16:46,313
Don't worry.

146
00:16:46,877 --> 00:16:48,100
I have a plan.

147
00:16:48,693 --> 00:16:49,693
Away!

148
00:16:51,439 --> 00:16:52,586
Your Highness...

149
00:16:54,839 --> 00:16:56,740
This is the end for Sapphire.

150
00:17:42,733 --> 00:17:45,313
Here it comes... It's tearing up the town.

151
00:18:03,364 --> 00:18:06,199
Hey, Moose! This time we settle the score!

152
00:18:44,536 --> 00:18:45,560
Sapphire! Look out!

153
00:19:01,220 --> 00:19:02,120
Alright!

154
00:19:02,124 --> 00:19:03,993
Don't kill it! It's in its neck!

155
00:19:04,100 --> 00:19:05,286
Pull out the blowdart!

156
00:19:14,399 --> 00:19:16,820
Didn't Tink just mention a blowdart?

157
00:19:18,220 --> 00:19:18,840
This is it!

158
00:19:44,369 --> 00:19:45,539
Sapphire!

159
00:19:46,049 --> 00:19:48,480
Rin-chan, hurry up and bring the vine!

160
00:19:51,679 --> 00:19:53,360
Bring more! Lots more!

161
00:19:59,486 --> 00:20:02,606
Everyone, tie those ends to the trees!

162
00:20:02,745 --> 00:20:03,745
Ready?

163
00:20:23,077 --> 00:20:24,137
Sapphire!

164
00:20:24,471 --> 00:20:25,931
Hold on tight!

165
00:20:52,124 --> 00:20:54,140
Moose, open your eyes.

166
00:20:54,679 --> 00:20:56,700
Sapphire pulled out the blowdart for you.

167
00:21:08,180 --> 00:21:09,180
Moose!

168
00:21:10,659 --> 00:21:13,800
An evil human poisoned you.

169
00:21:13,924 --> 00:21:16,586
This is the person who saved you.

170
00:21:18,874 --> 00:21:20,260
He's saying thank you.

171
00:21:21,599 --> 00:21:23,420
I'm the one who should apologize, Moose.

172
00:21:24,244 --> 00:21:26,379
To think I ever tried to get rid of you...

173
00:21:41,839 --> 00:21:42,730
Oh? What's this?

174
00:21:44,695 --> 00:21:48,286
Nylon, didn't Sapphire capture Moose?

175
00:21:49,024 --> 00:21:52,898
No, that can't be! I definitely hit his neck with a poison dart!

176
00:21:52,922 --> 00:21:56,486
You utter fool! Go do a handstand on top of that tower!

177
00:21:56,644 --> 00:21:58,300
Whaaat? Fine, I'll just try it one more time!

178
00:22:01,219 --> 00:22:02,765
When Moose gets close—<i>thwip! stab!</i>

179
00:22:02,789 --> 00:22:04,840
Then Moose will run right over Sapphire and trample him to death!

180
00:22:07,029 --> 00:22:09,029
Bye-bye!

181
00:22:26,507 --> 00:22:27,805
Darn it!

182
00:22:27,829 --> 00:22:29,925
Hey, wait!

183
00:22:29,949 --> 00:22:32,333
Wait, aren't you that old man?!

184
00:22:50,036 --> 00:22:54,222
Mommy!

185
00:23:10,979 --> 00:23:13,972
Sapphire really isn't a coward after all.

186
00:23:13,996 --> 00:23:16,052
She's so strong and cool!

187
00:23:16,076 --> 00:23:19,400
That's not all—she's brave and kind, too.

188
00:23:21,569 --> 00:23:25,900
Lord Sapphire, do you think Moose made it back to the forest safely?

189
00:23:27,369 --> 00:23:29,480
I was just thinking about that myself.

190
00:23:31,849 --> 00:23:32,418
Moose,

191
00:23:34,076 --> 00:23:36,000
stay healthy and safe forever.

192
00:23:36,430 --> 00:23:37,484

